   "source": [
    "### Conclusions:\n",
    "Total bill shows a strong positive correlation with tip, indicating that customers tend to tip more as the bill amount increases.<br>\n",
    "**Smoker vs Non-Smoker**\n",
    "No significant difference in tipping behavior between smokers and non-smokers.<br>\n",
    "However, smokers may show slightly higher variability.<br>\n",
    "**Gender vs Spending**\n",
    "Male customers show slightly higher total bills and greater variability.<br>\n",
    "However, difference is not very significant.<br>\n",
    "**Day-wise Behavior**\n",
    "Weekend days (especially Saturday & Sunday) show higher total bills.<br>\n",
    "Indicates higher spending activity on weekends.<br>\n",
    "**Time (Lunch vs Dinner)**\n",
    "Dinner time has higher total bills compared to lunch.<br>\n",
    "Suggests higher revenue generation in evenings.<br>\n",
    "**Group Size Impact**\n",
    "Larger groups tend to have higher total bills.<br>\n",
    "However, tip percentage slightly decreases as group size increases.<br>"
   ]
