    "\n",
    "**What if I don't drop any category?** Suppose you intentionally write: OneHotEncoder(drop=None)<br>\n",
    "Scikit-learn will still fit the model because modern implementations can handle this numerically, but:<br>\n",
    "The coefficients become not uniquely identifiable.They become harder to interpret.Some coefficients may be unstable because of multicollinearity.<br>\n",
    "This is why, for linear models, we usually drop one category.<br>\n",
    "\n",
    "### Rules to Remember:\n",
    "\n",
    "For a categorical feature with k categories:\n",
    "\n",
    "One-hot encoding creates k columns.\n",
    "For linear regression, we usually drop one column.\n",
    "The dropped category becomes the reference category.\n",
    "Every remaining coefficient tells you the change relative to that reference.\n",
    "Changing the reference changes the coefficient values, not the model's predictions."
   ]
