  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6b7ea1f2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "| Train R²             | Test R²          | Interpretation |\n",
    "| -------------------- | ---------------- | -------------- |\n",
    "| High                 | High             | Good fit       |\n",
    "| High                 | Low              | Overfitting    |\n",
    "| Low                  | Low              | Underfitting   |\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why Do We Compare Train and Test R²?**\n",
    "\n",
    "The training score tells us:\n",
    "\n",
    "How well does the model fit the data it has already seen?\n",
    "\n",
    "The test score tells us:\n",
    "\n",
    "How well does it perform on completely unseen data?\n",
    "\n",
    "The gap between them is often more informative than the scores themselves.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d59b5c25",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Use Cross Validation (Instead of Trusting One Split)**<br>\n",
    "\n",
    "After you've compared models on one train/test split, the next improvement is to estimate how they perform across multiple splits."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 88,
   "id": "3a671f08",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Linear Regression Mean R²: 0.39859369421350166\n",
      "Decision Tree Regressor Mean R²: -0.12317403707828978\n",
      "Random Forest Regressor Mean R²: 0.38419407104628206\n",
      "Gradient Boosting Regressor Mean R²: 0.3695669920361301\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.model_selection import cross_val_score, KFold\n",
    "\n",
    "cv = KFold(n_splits=10, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n",
    "\n",
    "models = {\n",
    "    'Linear Regression': LinearRegression(),\n",
    "    'Decision Tree Regressor': DecisionTreeRegressor(random_state=42),\n",
    "    'Random Forest Regressor': RandomForestRegressor(random_state=42),\n",
    "    'Gradient Boosting Regressor': GradientBoostingRegressor(random_state=42)\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "for name, model in models.items():\n",
    "    pipe = Pipeline([\n",
    "        ('preprocess', preprocessor),\n",
    "        ('model', model)\n",
    "    ])\n",
    "\n",
    "    scores = cross_val_score(pipe, X, y, cv=cv, scoring='r2')\n",
    "    print(name, \"Mean R²:\", scores.mean())"
   ]
  },
